@page "/docs/components/tree"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Tree
<PageTitle>Tree - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Tree</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="tree" />
        </div>
        <p>A data-driven tree view that follows the WAI-ARIA treeview pattern, with full keyboard navigation and typeahead. You bind your own items and the tree renders the hierarchy, with single or multiple selection, tri-state checkboxes, lazy loading, rename and search available as parameters.</p>
        <p>Drag and drop can reorder nodes, move them under a new parent or hand them to another tree, by pointer or entirely by keyboard. The tree never changes your data itself: every committed drop is reported as a <span class="font-mono text-sm">TreeChange</span> that you apply.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(TreeUsageExample)"
                Description="Bind `Items` with a `ValueSelector`, and add a `ChildrenSelector` for nesting. Expansion, selection and checks are all bindable lists of values. Every example below uses this `TreeItem` class and its `File` and `Folder` helpers." />

    <CompositionTree Root="Anatomy"
                     Description="The tree is a single component that renders these parts from your data. Each branch is a focusable `treeitem` that wraps its row and a group of children, while each leaf is a single row. Style the parts through their `data-part` attributes." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Default" Description="A file explorer. Click a branch row or its chevron to expand it, and click any row to select it. From the keyboard, Up and Down move, Right expands and enters a branch, Left collapses it or moves to the parent, Home and End jump to the ends, Enter selects, typing a letter jumps by name and * expands all siblings." Example="typeof(TreeDefaultExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Expand on click" Description="By default, clicking a branch row both selects it and toggles its expansion. Set `ExpandOnClick` to `false` to keep expansion on the chevron, so a click on the row only selects it. The keyboard splits the same way: Enter and Space only select, while the Right and Left arrows still expand and collapse." Example="typeof(TreeExpandOnClickExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Multiple selection" Description="With `SelectionMode` set to `Multiple`, a plain click or Enter replaces the selection, Ctrl+Click toggles a node, Shift+Click selects the visible range and Ctrl+A selects everything. To pick nodes that are not adjacent from the keyboard, move with the arrows and press Space on each one." Example="typeof(TreeMultipleExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Checkboxes" Description="`Checkable` adds a tri-state checkbox to every node, and Space toggles the focused one. The bound list holds the checked leaf values. A branch shows checked, mixed or unchecked based on its subtree, and checking a branch toggles everything under it." Example="typeof(TreeCheckboxExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Custom node template" Description="`NodeContent` replaces the default text with your own row content and receives the full state of the node, from its item and depth to its expansion, selection, check and loading state. The chevron and checkbox stay in place, and everything after them is yours. Here each row gets a file icon, a badge with the child count and a dropdown menu whose wrapper stops clicks and keys from selecting the row." Example="typeof(TreeTemplateExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Lazy loading" Description="Mark unloaded branches with `HasChildrenSelector` and supply `LoadChildren`. It runs the first time a branch expands, showing a spinner in place of the chevron and setting `aria-busy` on the row, and the result is cached. Expand a planet to fetch its moons." Example="typeof(TreeLazyExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Drag and drop" Description="Set `Draggable` to let any row be picked up. With a pointer, drop on the top or bottom edge of a row to place the node before or after it, or on the middle of a branch to drop it inside. From the keyboard, Ctrl+Space grabs the focused node, the arrow keys move it, Ctrl+Space or Enter drops it and Escape cancels. Here `CanDrag` keeps index.html in place." Example="typeof(TreeDragExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Drag between trees" Description="Give two trees the same `Group` to drag nodes between them with a pointer. The source tree raises `OnMove` and the receiving tree raises `OnReceive`. Each tree has an `Id`, so one handler can tell the sides apart and apply the change to both lists." Example="typeof(TreeCrossTreeExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Controlled expansion" Description="`ExpandedValues` is a bindable list, and a component reference gives you methods such as `ExpandAllAsync`, `CollapseAllAsync`, `ExpandAsync` and `FocusNodeAsync`. The buttons here call them, while the tree stays fully usable from the keyboard." Example="typeof(TreeControlledExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Rename" Description="Set `Renamable`, then press F2 on a focused row or double-click it to edit its name inline. Enter or clicking away commits and raises `OnRename`, while Escape cancels. `CanRename` makes exceptions for individual nodes, which is why the Inbox folder here keeps its name." Example="typeof(TreeRenameExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Disabled nodes" Description="`DisabledSelector` disables individual nodes. They stay visible and the arrow keys still reach them, so screen reader users still hear them, but they cannot be selected, checked, dragged or expanded. `Disabled` on the tree turns off every node." Example="typeof(TreeDisabledExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Search" Description="`Searchable` adds a filter box above the tree. As you type, it keeps the matching nodes and the folders leading to them, opens those folders and highlights the matches. Clearing the box restores the tree and your own expansion, and state such as checks survives filtering. Bind `Search` to drive it from code, or pass `SearchMatch` for custom matching." Example="typeof(TreeSearchExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Virtualization" Description="For long trees, `Virtualize` renders only the rows in and around the visible area, so the DOM stays small however many nodes there are. This tree holds 1,000 nodes, and the keyboard and search box still reach all of them. Give the tree a fixed height and overflow. Virtualization throws when combined with `Draggable` or when rows differ from `ItemSize`, and guides fall back to indentation." Example="typeof(TreeVirtualExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Guide lines" Description="`Guides` sets how the hierarchy is drawn. `None` relies on indentation alone, and `Lines`, the default, runs a vertical guide along the children of each branch. `Connectors` stops the guide at the last child and adds a rounded horizontal branch to each row." Example="typeof(TreeGuidesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization" Description="Every part accepts plain Tailwind classes, so the look does not have to come from the theme tokens. This example uses a slate container with a blue accent for hover, focus and selection, and `Indent` widens the offset for each level." Example="typeof(TreeCustomExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Marquee labels"
          Description="With `Marquee`, a label cut off by an ellipsis slides its hidden end into view while hovered, then slides back. Labels that fit are left alone, and readers who prefer reduced motion get an instant reveal instead of the slide."
          Example="typeof(TreeMarqueeExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL" Description="Set `Dir` to `Rtl`, or inherit it from a `DirectionProvider`, and the whole tree mirrors. Indentation grows from the right, the guide lines and chevron flip, and the Left and Right arrows swap roles for expanding and collapsing. Custom node templates mirror with it." Example="typeof(TreeRtlExample)" />
</div>

@code {
    private static readonly CompositionNode Anatomy = new("BzTree",
        new CompositionNode("branch (treeitem)",
            new CompositionNode("branch-control (row)",
                new CompositionNode("indicator"),
                new CompositionNode("checkbox"),
                new CompositionNode("text / NodeContent")),
            new CompositionNode("branch-content (group)",
                new CompositionNode("... nested branches and items"))),
        new CompositionNode("item (leaf row)"));
}
